# Development Workflow Rule

## 1) Start With Plan
- Clarify requirements before coding when scope is ambiguous.
- Break work into explicit to-dos and track progress from first to last task.

## 2) Branching Strategy
- Create a new branch for each feature/fix (e.g., `feat/...`, `fix/...`).
- Do not implement feature work directly on `main`.

## 3) Implementation Quality
- Keep changes scoped to the requested feature.
- Reuse existing project patterns and naming conventions.
- Avoid committing runtime/local artifacts (`node_modules`, local DB files, logs, debug/session files, secrets).

## 4) Verification Before Commit
- Run quick syntax/lint checks for changed files.
- If available, run relevant test/build commands for touched areas.
- Fix obvious issues before creating a commit.

## 5) Git Hygiene
- Stage only relevant files.
- Write commit messages that describe user value (why), not only file changes.
- Push feature branch to origin with upstream tracking.

## 6) Pull Request Standard
- Open PR from feature branch to `main`.
- PR body must include:
  - Summary (what changed and why)
  - Test plan checklist (how to verify)

## 7) Merge Preference
- Default merge method: **Squash merge** for a clean `main` history.
- After merge, delete merged feature branch when safe.
